heading('4.28 Summary',2); p('The implementation combines a Flask web backend, Jinja/Bootstrap interfaces, SQLAlchemy models and a Vercel deployment configuration. The design is intentionally modular. Confirmed code capabilities are documented separately from features that depend on external services, configuration, testing or future development.')

chapter('CHAPTER FIVE: SYSTEM TESTING AND EVALUATION')
heading('5.1 Introduction',2); p('Testing verifies that a feature meets its defined acceptance criterion and that access restrictions, messages and data state behave as expected. The “Actual Result” and “Status” fields below are deliberately left for execution evidence; they must not be marked passed without a recorded test run.')
heading('5.2 Testing Methodology',2); p('Use a layered approach: manual functional tests for user workflows; role/ownership tests for access control; usability sessions with representative users; security checks for authentication, input handling and protected files; and performance/deployment tests in an environment representative of release. Record test date, tester, build/commit identifier, browser/device, input data and evidence for each result.')
heading('5.3 Functional Testing',2)
tests=[('TC-01','Registration','Submit valid and duplicate account data.','Valid account is created; duplicate data receives a clear error.'),('TC-02','Login','Login with valid and invalid credentials.','Authorised user reaches correct dashboard; invalid login is rejected.'),('TC-03','Appointment booking','Select provider and available slot, then submit.','Appointment is stored with correct patient, provider and status.'),('TC-04','Appointment cancellation','Cancel an owned scheduled appointment.','Status/action changes according to business rule; unauthorised user is rejected.'),('TC-05','Queue tracking','Join queue and inspect position/status.','Queue record has number, status and estimated wait.'),('TC-06','Provider search','Search/browse provider records.','Matching provider profiles are displayed.'),('TC-07','Pharmacy','Place valid medicine order with prescription condition.','Order is stored; stock/prescription conditions are respected.'),('TC-08','Laboratory','Submit laboratory booking request.','Booking is stored with requested test and status.'),('TC-09','Payments','Invoke appointment payment workflow.','Internal status/reference updates; do not test with real funds unless gateway is verified.'),('TC-10','Family accounts','Add and remove authorised family-member record.','Ownership is enforced and record changes correctly.'),('TC-11','AI helper','Submit common and urgent symptom prompts.','Informational response and clear non-diagnostic/escalation notice are shown.'),('TC-12','Language switching','Switch each supported locale on representative pages.','All visible interface text is translated or defects are logged.'),('TC-13','Notifications','Create/read notification for intended user.','Notification visibility and read state are correct.'),('TC-14','Admin functions','Access management screens with admin and patient accounts.','Admin succeeds; non-admin receives denial/redirect.')]
table(['Test ID','Feature','Test Description','Expected Result','Actual Result','Status'],[[a,b,c,e,'[INSERT RESULT]','[PASS/FAIL]'] for a,b,c,e in tests],[.55,.9,2.05,2.05,1.2,.65])
heading('5.4 Usability Testing',2); p('Recruit [INSERT NUMBER] representative users and ask each to register, find a provider, book an appointment, check a queue, request a service and change language. Collect task completion, observed errors, time on task and qualitative feedback. Evaluate clarity of labels, navigation, forms, confirmation messages, mobile responsiveness and translation quality. [INSERT USABILITY RESULTS AND IMPROVEMENTS.]')
heading('5.5 Security Testing',2); p('Test unauthenticated access to protected routes; attempt cross-user access to appointments, records and payments; validate invalid login/reset tokens; inspect session-cookie attributes in production; test file-upload type/size handling; and verify that secrets are supplied by environment configuration rather than committed. Do not perform intrusive testing against systems without authorisation. [INSERT SECURITY TEST EVIDENCE AND FINDINGS.]')
heading('5.6 Performance Testing',2); p('Measure representative page and action response times under an agreed workload. Include home page, login, dashboard, appointment submission, queue update and language switch. Record network conditions, dataset size, concurrency, percentile response times and errors. [INSERT TOOL, ENVIRONMENT AND RESULTS.]')
heading('5.7 Test Results',2); table(['Area','Result to record','Decision'],[['Functional workflows','[INSERT PASS/FAIL COUNT AND DEFECT IDS]','[INSERT ACCEPT/RETEST]'],['Usability','[INSERT COMPLETION/FEEDBACK SUMMARY]','[INSERT ACCEPT/IMPROVE]'],['Security','[INSERT FINDINGS/REMEDIATION]','[INSERT ACCEPT/BLOCK]'],['Performance','[INSERT MEASUREMENTS]','[INSERT ACCEPT/TUNE]'],['Localisation','[INSERT LANGUAGE COVERAGE AUDIT]','[INSERT ACCEPT/COMPLETE TRANSLATIONS]']])
heading('5.8 Deployment Testing',2); p('After deployment to Vercel, test the public URL, routing, static assets, authentication, database persistence, file storage behaviour, environment variables, HTTPS, logs and error paths. Vercel’s serverless filesystem is not a durable database location; verify that production database configuration and upload strategy meet the application’s needs. [INSERT DEPLOYMENT TEST DATE, URL, COMMIT AND RESULTS.]')
heading('5.9 Summary',2); p('The test plan supplies traceability for the principal functions and protects against unsupported claims. The report should be finalised only after actual outcomes and defect resolutions have been inserted.')

chapter('CHAPTER SIX: CONCLUSION AND RECOMMENDATIONS')
heading('6.1 Introduction',2); p('This chapter summarises the project, maps objectives to evidence and identifies responsible next steps.')
heading('6.2 Summary of the Project',2); p('The project developed an integrated healthcare service management web application for coordinating patient and administrative workflows through a browser. The documented solution includes identity and role management, appointment and queue workflows, provider information, service-request modules, communication features, localisation support and administration. It uses a Python/Flask architecture with Jinja, SQLAlchemy, a local SQLite configuration and a Vercel deployment configuration. The project is a web application only.')
heading('6.3 Achievement of Objectives',2)
table(['Table 6.1: Objective','Achievement evidence','Status'],[['Authentication and roles','User model, password hashing, login routes and role checks.','Implemented; deployment hardening required.'],['Appointments and queues','Appointment, slot and QueueRecord models/routes.','Implemented; validate deployed behaviour.'],['Provider/service access','Provider, pharmacy, laboratory, records and family modules.','Implemented in source; operational integrations require confirmation.'],['Information helpers','AI chat and symptom-checker routes.','Implemented as informational helpers only; not clinical diagnosis.'],['Multilingual interface','Language preferences and eight listed locale options/catalogues.','Architecture implemented; full-string coverage must be audited.'],['Administration','Admin, pharmacy, announcement and analytics routes/templates.','Implemented in source; verify permissions and reports.'],['Web deployment/version control','Vercel config; Git repository present.','Vercel configured; insert live URL and GitHub link.']])
heading('6.4 Conclusion',2); p('The project demonstrates a coherent approach to healthcare-service management on the web. Its principal contribution is the integration of service-oriented workflows within a role-based, responsive application rather than a collection of unrelated pages. The system should be assessed as a software-management platform: it can organise requests, information and communication, but it does not replace clinical judgement, emergency services, regulated payment processing or institutional governance. Completion of the verification checklist and production safeguards is essential before real-world deployment involving sensitive health data.')
heading('6.5 Recommendations',2); p('Prioritise a production database, secret management, HTTPS verification, secure upload storage, backup/retention policy, audit trails, accessibility testing and a full translation audit. Establish data-protection, consent, clinical escalation, provider verification and incident-response policies with the relevant healthcare institution before handling real patient data. Replace the internal payment-status simulation with a properly approved payment-provider integration only when the necessary business and compliance arrangements are in place.')
heading('6.6 Future Enhancements',2)
for x in ['Develop a dedicated mobile application as future work; it is not part of the current project.','Integrate approved wearable devices and patient-consented remote-monitoring workflows.','Add additional verified payment providers and transaction reconciliation.','Introduce advanced, clinically governed AI capabilities with validation, monitoring, fairness assessment and clinician oversight.','Support ambulance tracking and verified emergency dispatch integration subject to local authority approval.','Integrate additional healthcare institutions through documented interoperability agreements.','Add further languages and complete professional translation/quality assurance for all user-facing strings.']: bullet(x)

